.SH NAME
niac-scenario-list - List available scenarios and scenario packs


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac scenario list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print every bundled scenario name with a one-line description.
They are small, hand-written starting points (basic-network, captured-switch,
captured-pair, resource-pressure) and the fastest path to a runnable YAML config.
Scenario packs (hospital, warehouse, campus, ...) are listed after them; they
are generated with 'niac scenario generate'.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # List all scenarios with descriptions
  niac scenario list
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-scenario(1)\fP


